@page "/Account/AccessDenied"
@attribute [Authorize]

@* Static SSR. The cookie handler sends a signed-in caller here when a policy refuses them (its
   default AccessDeniedPath); without this page they got a 404. Plain [Authorize] (signed in, no
   MFA): only an authenticated caller is ever redirected here, and an Admin, Safeguarding Officer
   or Teacher without MFA must be able to read the enrolment link below (MfaRequirement). Same
   wording as Routes.razor's NotAuthorized content. *@

<PageTitle>Access denied</PageTitle>

<div class="auth">
<PageHeader Title="Access denied" />

<p role="alert">You are not authorized to view this page.</p>
<p>
    If your role requires two-factor authentication, set it up on the
    <a href="Account/Manage/TwoFactorAuthentication">two-factor authentication page</a>.
</p>
<p><a href="">Go to the home page</a></p>
</div>
